UPDATE companies SET description='Rockford Molded Products began in 1943 when Henry "Hank" Gustafson and Norman Johnson opened a tool-and-die shop in a garage on 18th Avenue in Rockford, Illinois. The fledgling operation produced components for the U.S. Army during World War II, joining the region''s broader wartime manufacturing effort. By the 1950s the partners had built their first injection molding machine from scratch, laying the groundwork for the company''s future focus on plastic molding.

Today the company operates from a facility in Rockford (Loves Park area) and offers plastic injection molding, custom fabrication, product assembly, Bridgeport milling, and quality control services. An in-house tool room supports mold development, and the shop also provides 3D printing for prototyping. No headcount or annual volume figures are published.

The firm does not list specific target industries on its website, though its early work was for military contracts. Current marketing emphasizes general plastic injection molding solutions for customers seeking production-scale or prototype parts.

Leadership stresses quality as a defining trait: the company holds ISO 9001:2015 certification and UL approval, maintains a quality management system with NIST-traceable calibration, and cites over 80 years of continuous operation as evidence of its commitment.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','UL-Approved']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection Molding", "Custom Fabrication", "Product Assembly", "Bridgeport Milling", "Quality Control", "3D Printing", "Quoting", "Tool Room Services"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Bridgeport milling machines", "Injection molding machines", "3D printers"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001:2015 certified and UL-approved", "Quality management system with NIST-traceable equipment calibration", "In-house tool room and injection molding machine building heritage", "Bridgeport milling and custom fabrication capabilities", "Over 80 years of continuous operation"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1943 by Henry ''Hank'' Gustafson and Norman Johnson in Rockford, IL -> /", "Started as tool and die shop making components for US Army during WWII -> /", "Built first injection molding machine in 1950s -> /", "Current address 5600 Pike Road, Rockford, IL 61111-4711 -> /", "Officers: Wayne Rasner Jr (COO), Tom Thome (CFO) -> /", "Certifications: ISO 9001:2015, UL-Approved -> /", "Services: Injection Molding, Custom Fabrication, Product Assembly, Bridgeport Milling, Quality Control, Quoting -> /", "3D Printing mentioned -> /services", "Quality Management System with NIST-traceable calibration -> /quality", "80+ years in business -> /quality", "Headquarters city Loves Park, Illinois -> db", "Founded year 1943 -> db and /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Rockford Molded was started back in 1943 by Henry ''Hank'' Gustafson & Norman Johnson it started in a small garage on 18th Avenue in Rockford, Illinois. At first it was a tool and die shop and they made components for the US Army during World War II...", "founded_year": "1943", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='rockford-molded-products-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Rocky Mountain Apparel has operated in Denver, Colorado for over 25 years, providing screen printing, embroidery, and promotional product services to businesses and events throughout the metro area.

The company specializes in high-quality plastisol, waterbase, and discharge screen printing on garments, accommodating runs from single pieces to 10,000-plus units with up to ten colors. Its embroidery department runs 40-head machines supported by in-house digitizing and editing, allowing both small and large-scale projects.

Clients range from local businesses and corporate buyers seeking branded apparel and employee gifts to event organizers needing custom merchandise. The shop serves individual customers as well, handling personal projects such as monogrammed jackets or hats.

