UPDATE companies SET description='Rocky Mountain Power operates from its headquarters in Casper, Wyoming, serving as an electric utility across a three-state territory. The company delivers power to more than 1.2 million customers in Utah, Wyoming, and Idaho, maintaining the infrastructure and service operations required for daily energy delivery.

The utility provides electric service connections, billing, and account management for residential, commercial, and industrial customers. Its operations include wildfire mitigation and system resiliency work, such as the ongoing projects on Casper Mountain to reduce fire risk and improve reliability. The company administers energy-efficiency rebates through its Wattsmart program, offers Time of Use rate plans, and runs the Blue Sky program for renewable energy support. It also maintains electric service requirements and approved meter equipment standards for builders and contractors.

Customers range from homeowners and small businesses to large industrial facilities and municipal projects. The utility works directly with builders and contractors on new construction, provides economic development resources to attract employers, and supports electric vehicle adoption through dedicated programs. Bill assistance and energy assistance programs are available for customers facing financial hardship.

Rocky Mountain Power emphasizes safety as its highest priority, with 24/7 operations to maintain reliability. The company states it is committed to keeping rates low, investing in system resilience, and supporting the communities it serves through its foundation and local initiatives.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electric service connections (start, stop, move)", "Electric service requirements and standards", "Approved meter service equipment specifications", "Wildfire mitigation and system resiliency work", "Energy-efficiency rebates (Wattsmart program)", "Time of Use rate plans", "Renewable energy program (Blue Sky)", "Electric vehicle programs and resources", "Economic development assistance", "Bill payment assistance and energy assistance", "Home energy reports and usage analysis", "Builder and contractor resources"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Construction/Builders", "Municipal/Government", "Economic development"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Safety-first priority with 24/7 operations", "Serves 1.2 million customers across Utah, Wyoming, and Idaho", "Wildfire mitigation and system resiliency investments", "Wattsmart energy-efficiency rebates and Blue Sky renewable program", "Economic development support for communities"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Casper, Wyoming -> db", "Serves 1.2 million customers in Utah, Wyoming, Idaho -> about page", "Wildfire mitigation work on Casper Mountain -> home page", "Wattsmart rebates program -> home page", "Blue Sky renewable energy program -> home page", "Time of Use plans -> home page", "Electric service requirements for builders/contractors -> home page", "Approved meter service equipment -> home page", "Economic development resources -> about page", "EV programs -> about page", "Bill assistance and energy assistance -> about page", "Rocky Mountain Power Foundation -> about page", "Safet