UPDATE companies SET description='S and Y Industries, Inc. is based in Winfield, Kansas. The company was founded in 1984 by Sandy Foust on the back porch of a farmhouse in nearby Atlanta, Kansas. It remains a family-owned and woman-owned business, with Foust serving as CEO and her sons Dan and John Foust overseeing production operations and sales.

The firm provides custom electronics engineering, manufacturing, and turnkey assembly services. Its capabilities include printed circuit board (PCB) assembly using surface mount technology (SMT) and thru-hole processes, wire harness assembly, electro-mechanical box-build integration, product test development, and functional testing. Operations run from a 60,000-square-foot facility staffed by more than 100 employees, supporting prototype through low- to mid-volume production runs.

The company has supplied companies in these industries for over 35 years, delivering precision electronic assemblies and complete box-build solutions.

S and Y Industries emphasizes a family-like culture, stating that "people who care about where they work make better products." The leadership describes its approach as acting as a seamless extension of the customer''s operation, aiming to provide what the customer wants, when they want it, without unnecessary questions.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 13485','AS9100D','ITAR Registered','IPC-A-610','J-STD-001','RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB assembly (SMT and thru-hole)", "PCB prototype production", "Wire harness assembly", "Electro-mechanical box-build assembly", "Electronics engineering and design (DFM/DFT)", "Hardware and software development for test", "Product test development and functional testing", "Incoming, in-process, and final inspection (IPC-A-610)", "3D Automated Optical Inspection (AOI)", "Program management and inventory solutions", "Material procurement and supply chain management", "New product introduction (NPI)", "Fulfillment, service, and repair", "Low- to mid-volume production"], "industries": ["Medical", "Aerospace", "Defense", "Commercial", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["3D Automated Optical Inspection systems"], "volume": "Prototype to low-mid volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and woman-led since 1984", "AS9100D and ISO 13485 certified for aerospace and medical applications", "ITAR registered for defense work", "60,000 sq ft facility with 100+ expert employees", "IPC-A-610 and J-STD-001 certified technicians on staff"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1984 by Sandy Foust on back porch in Atlanta, Kansas -> /about-us", "Relocated to Winfield, Kansas in 1989 -> /about-us", "60,000 sq ft facility, 100+ employees -> /about-us", "Family-owned, woman-owned; CEO Sandy Foust, sons Dan and John Foust -> /about-us", "Services: PCB assembly (SMT/thru-hole), wire harness, box-build, engineering, testing -> /services", "Industries: medical, aerospace, defense, commercial, industrial -> /about-us, /services", "Certifications: ISO 9001:2015, ISO 13485, AS9100D, ITAR Registered, IPC-A-610, J-STD-001, RoHS -> /quality", "3D Automated Optical Inspection systems -> /services", "Volume: prototype to low-mid volume -> /services", "Company type: electronic contract manufacturer -> /services"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "S and Y Industries is an electronic contract manufacturer offering complete turnkey solutions including electronic design, printed circuit boards and more.", "founded_year": "1984", "employee_count": "100+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR Registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned", "Woman-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='s-and-y-industries-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='S&F Foods, Inc. was founded in 2003 and is headquartered in Romulus, Michigan, a suburb of Detroit. The company began as a manufacturer focused on institutional school foodservice programs and retail channels, producing a variety of enrobed and topped frozen items.

The company operates a 37,000-square-foot food manufacturing facility capable of handling both high and low production volumes. Its processing lines include an enrobed line for filling and par-baking hand-held pocket-style items, a topped line for par-baking crusts of various sizes, and individually quick frozen (IQF) capabilities. The facility also offers gluten-free manufacturing with segregated storage and a dedicated processing line, along with multiple packing options such as printed film, retail boxes, and cartons.

S&F Foods serves institutional school foodservice programs, retail distributors, and the National School Lunch Program across the United States. It also participates in USDA Commodity Processing for cheese, tomato paste, and flour. Signature products include the Original “Pull-A-Part” Topped Breadsticks and Dave’s Detroit Style Pizza™.

The company emphasizes food safety and quality, holding BRCGS AA Grade certification, GFCO gluten-free certification, and organic certification through the Global Organic Alliance. Its mission highlights a commitment to producing safe, certified, and authentic products, supported by in-house and external allergen testing and ongoing review of its Food Safety & Quality Policy.', certifications=ARRAY['BRCGS AA Grade','USDA','GFCO (Gluten Free)','Global Organic Alliance (Organic)','National Bioengineered Food Disclosure Statement']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Enrobed line (fill and par-bake hand-held pocket items)", "Topped line (top and par-bake crusts)", "Individually Quick Frozen (IQF)", "Mix hot or cold sauces", "Multiple packing options (printed film, retail box, carton)", "Gluten-free manufacturing (segregated storage, dedicated processing line)", "In-house allergen testing", "External allergen testing", "USDA Commodity Processing (cheese, tomato paste, flour)"], "industries": ["Institutional school foodservice", "Retail", "National School Lunch Program", "USDA Commodity Processing"], "materials": ["Cheese", "Tomato paste", "Flour", "Gluten-free ingredients"], "equipment": ["Enrobed line", "Topped line", "IQF (Individually Quick Frozen) equipment", "Packing equipment (printed film, retail box, carton)"], "volume": "High or low volume", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["BRCGS AA Grade certification", "Gluten-free manufacturing with segregated storage and dedicated line", "In-house and external allergen testing", "USDA Commodity Processing for cheese, tomato paste, flour", "Individually Quick Frozen (IQF) capability"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2003 -> db", "Headquartered in Romulus, Michigan -> /", "37,000 sq. ft. facility -> /capabilities", "Enrobed line, topped line, IQF, gluten-free manufacturing -> /capabilities", "BRCGS AA Grade, GFCO, Global Organic Alliance certifications -> /capabilities", "Serves institutional school foodservice, retail, National School Lunch Program -> /", "USDA Commodity Processing for cheese, tomato paste, flour -> /capabilities", "Products: Original Pull-A-Part Topped Breadsticks, Dave''s Detroit Style Pizza -> /", "Mission: safe, certified, authentic products -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Manufacturing for institutional school foodservice programs and retail since 2003.", "founded_year": "2003", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='s-f-foods-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='S&W Foods, operating as S&W Wholesale, was founded in 1978 by Frank and Rosemary Spalitta in Hammond, Louisiana. The family-owned business began with a focus on serving foodservice operators throughout Tangipahoa Parish. Today, the company is led by their son, Paul Spalitta, representing second-generation ownership with a third generation emerging.

The company functions as a broadline distributor, supplying a wide range of food and non-food items including produce, meats, breads, condiments, equipment, smallwares, paper goods, and cleaning supplies. Its distribution facility is located near the I-55/I-12 corridor, enabling rapid delivery across southeast Louisiana and the Mississippi Gulf Coast. S&W maintains private-label brands such as Copper Creek Cattle Company and Captain Frank''s Seafood, and partners with major suppliers including Unipro Foodservice, Campbell Foodservice, ConAgra Foodservice, Rich Products Corporation, Pillsbury, Hormel, General Mills, and Smithfield Foods.

S&W serves a diverse customer base of independent and chain restaurants, including donut shops, coffee shops, Tex-Mex, Italian, Mediterranean, family dining, sandwich shops, and seafood establishments. The company emphasizes personal relationships and quick response times, noting it remained operational and made deliveries the day after Hurricanes Ida and Katrina when other distributors could not.

The company''s guiding principle, coined by the founder, is "Large enough to serve, small enough to care." S&W differentiates itself through independent ownership that allows flexibility without corporate red tape, a commitment to knowing customers by name, and specialized programs such as custom-cut steaks, fresh produce sourcing through Fresh Concepts, and artisanal cheeses via The Rind Cheese Company.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Broadline foodservice distribution", "Private label brand management", "Custom-cut steak program", "Fresh produce sourcing and distribution", "Artisanal cheese selection and cutting", "Online ordering platform", "Emergency/disaster response delivery", "Brand-specific program development"], "industries": ["Foodservice distribution", "Restaurant supply", "Hospitality", "Independent restaurants", "Chain restaurants", "Donut shops", "Coffee shops", "Tex-Mex restaurants", "Italian restaurants", "Mediterranean restaurants", "Family dining", "Sandwich shops", "Seafood restaurants"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Independent, family-owned structure enabling quick decisions without corporate red tape", "Next-day delivery capability after natural disasters (demonstrated after Hurricanes Ida and Katrina)", "Private-label brands including Copper Creek Cattle Company and Captain Frank''s Seafood", "Partnership with Unipro Foodservice, the largest foodservice distribution cooperative in the U.S.", "Specialized programs for custom-cut steaks, fresh produce, and artisanal cheeses"], "facts_used": ["Company name S&W Foods -> db", "Founded 1978 by Frank & Rosemary Spalitta -> db, /", "Headquarters Hammond, Louisiana -> db, /", "Family-owned, second/third generation leadership -> /, /about-us", "Broadline distributor of food and non-food items -> /, /about-us", "Facility near I-55/I-12 corridor -> /", "Service area southeast Louisiana and Mississippi Gulf Co