UPDATE companies SET description='Sag Harbor Industries, Inc. was founded in 1946 by Charles Edison, son of inventor Thomas Edison, in Sag Harbor, New York. The company began with a single goal: to manufacture electrical coils and inductors of superior quality. Today it operates from two U.S. locations — its original headquarters in Sag Harbor, NY, and a second facility in Farmville, North Carolina.

The company produces custom power, control, and instrumentation transformers and coils, along with cable assemblies, printed circuit board assemblies, and full box-build services. Its product line includes toroidal, solenoid, electric, field, encapsulated, molded, self-supported, and varnished coils, supported by UL-recognized insulation systems. Multiple domestic plants run automated and semi-automated equipment, allowing the firm to handle high-volume, medium-volume, and short-run orders.

Sag Harbor serves the electronics, aerospace, medical device, renewable energy, industrial automation, and automotive sectors. Aerospace customers receive UL-compliant components built to AS9100 standards; medical clients get burr-free, high-precision coils for implants and diagnostic equipment under ISO 13485; renewable energy projects use toroidal coils and transformers for solar and wind installations; and automation firms source durable solenoid coils and cable assemblies for robotics and machinery.

The founder''s original quality mandate remains the company''s differentiator. Management cites 100% U.S. manufacturing, ISO 9001:2015, AS9100, and ISO 13485 certifications, engineering and design competence, flexible supply-chain management, and on-time delivery as the pillars of its "Sag Harbor Advantage."', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AS9100','ISO 13485']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Coil winding", "Transformer manufacturing", "Cable assembly", "PCB assembly", "Box build assembly", "Encapsulation", "Injection and transfer molding", "Varnishing (dipped, brushed, sprayed, vacuum impregnated)", "UL insulation systems", "Custom design and engineering", "Prototyping", "High volume production", "Medium volume production", "Short run production"], "industries": ["Electronics", "Aerospace", "Medical devices", "Renewable energy", "Industrial automation", "Automotive"], "materials": ["Magnet wire (copper base)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "High volume, medium volume, and short run production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% Made in USA manufacturing", "ISO 9001:2015, AS9100, and ISO 13485 certified", "Multiple U.S. locations with automated and semi-automated equipment", "High volume, medium volume, and short run production capabilities", "Engineering & design competence with flexible supply chain management"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1946 by Charles Edison -> db", "Headquarters Sag Harbor, NY and Farmville, NC -> /", "Products: custom transformers, coils, cable assemblies, PCB & box build -> /", "Coil types: toroidal, solenoid, electric, field, encapsulated, molded, self-supported, varnished -> /", "UL insulation systems -> /", "Automated/semi-automated equipment, high/medium/short run production -> /", "Industries: electronics, aerospace, medical, renewable energy, industrial automation, automotive -> /", "Certifications: ISO 9001:2015, AS9100, ISO 13485 -> /", "100% Made in USA -> /", "Engineering & design competence, flexible supply chain, on-time delivery -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our multiple U.S. manufacturing locations are equipped with state of art automated and semi-automated equipment.", "founded_year": "1946", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/sag-harbor-industries/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sag-harbor-industries-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sage Plastics, Inc. operates from its headquarters in Fort Worth, Texas, with a manufacturing network that includes a long-standing plant in Long Beach, California, and a newer facility in Colton, California. The Long Beach location has served the region for nearly 18 years as of 2023, while the Colton site joined the company in 2023 through the acquisition of Microdyne. A greenfield plant in Fort Worth was opened in 2022 to expand geographic reach into the Midwest and Southeast.

The company specializes in blow molding and injection molding of high-density polyethylene (HDPE) bottles and plastic containers. Its Long Beach plant focuses on core product lines for industrial, chemical, and foodservice markets, and holds IMS certification for dairy and beverage applications. The Colton facility adds injection molding capability alongside blow molding, with extensive customization options. Across all sites, Sage Plastics employs Statistical Quality Control (SPC) methods, special product testing, and a dedicated logistics department to manage shipping. The company emphasizes speed to market and food safety compliance.

Sage Plastics serves the dairy, beverage, foodservice, industrial, chemical, and household sectors. Its containers are used for food and beverage packaging, industrial chemicals, and reusable consumer bottles. The company positions itself as a preferred supplier for businesses seeking high-volume output without excessive lead times or administrative burden.

