UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Nashville, Tennessee, Sattler Manufacturing operates as a custom metal fabrication shop serving the Middle Tennessee region. The company combines decades of industrial fabrication experience with modern metal shop technologies, including laser cutting, to produce custom parts, equipment, and structures.

The shop works with stainless steel, aluminum, and mild steel, offering processes such as laser cutting, shearing, bending, welding, and forming. In addition to fabrication, Sattler provides in-house design and engineering support, including CAD drawing conversion, 3D solid modeling, value engineering, and project management. The team also handles industrial maintenance, pipefitting, and on-site installation of replacement equipment.

Industrial engineering, operations, plant maintenance, and safety managers throughout Middle Tennessee rely on Sattler for projects ranging from material handling systems and piping to structural frames, food processing equipment, and machine guarding. The company''s customer base includes manufacturers, machinists, and engineers who need prototype runs as well as production quantities.

Sattler emphasizes its blend of long-standing fabrication expertise with current laser technology to deliver fast, affordable custom metalwork. The firm states that its engineers and fabricators work hand-in-hand with clients to ensure every project meets specifications, budget, and schedule.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Laser cutting", "Metal shearing", "Metal bending", "Welding", "Metal forming", "Custom metal fabrication", "Structural fabrication", "Equipment fabrication", "Design engineering", "CAD/CAM support", "3D solid modeling", "Value engineering", "Project management", "Industrial maintenance", "Pipefitting", "On-site installation", "Prototyping", "Assembly", "Manufacturability design review", "Jig and fixture design"], "industries": ["Food processing", "Manufacturing", "Material handling", "Piping", "Structural fabrication", "Industrial maintenance", "Safety equipment", "Machine operations", "Industrial engineering"], "materials": ["Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Mild steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Decades of fabrication experience paired with modern laser cutting technology", "In-house design and engineering support including CAD and 3D modeling", "Full-service industrial maintenance and pipefitting", "Fast and affordable custom laser cutting for stainless steel, aluminum, and mild steel", "On-site installation and equipment replacement services"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Nashville, Tennessee -> db", "Custom metal fabrication shop offering laser cutting, shearing, bending, welding, forming -> /", "Materials: stainless steel, aluminum, mild steel -> /", "Industries served: industrial engineering, operations, plant maintenance, safety managers in Middle Tennessee; material handling, piping, structural, food processing, manufacturing, safety, machine operations -> /", "Design and engineering services: CAD support, 3D solid modeling, value engineering, project management -> /services", "Industrial maintenance, pipefitting, on-site installation -> /", "Software used: Trumpf TruTops, SolidWorks, AutoCAD, DraftSight -> /services", "No founding year, ownership type, employee count, certifications, volume, lead time, tolerances stated -> db, /, /about, /services"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Sattler Manufacturing is the trusted custom metal fabrication shop of Nashville, Tennessee.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sattler-manufacturing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Savannah Food Company, based in Savannah, Tennessee, traces its roots to 1970 when Bob Hagy, after decades in the restaurant business, began producing hushpuppies from his family’s recipes. The Catfish Hotel Restaurant, still operating today, had built a reputation for its freshly made hushpuppies, prompting Hagy to build a dedicated processing facility. In 2004, the company was acquired by John Bryan, whose family had founded Bryan Foods, Inc., in the early 1900s.

Production follows a strict hazard analysis and critical control point (HACCP) plan, good manufacturing practices (GMP), and global food safety initiative (GFSI) benchmarks. The plant has held FSSC 22000 certification since June 2013, aligning with ISO-based food safety standards.

The company sells its products through retail stores, as indicated by a store locator on its website, distributing under the Savannah Classics brand.

The business emphasizes its commitment to food safety and quality, citing its FSSC 22000 certification, HACCP/GMP/GFSI systems, and the use of high-quality ingredients to replicate scratch-made flavor. The operation was built on family recipes passed down through generations, aiming to deliver products as good as homemade.', certifications=ARRAY['FSSC 22000']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Food processing", "Hushpuppy production", "Side dish manufacturing", "HACCP plan implementation", "GMP compliance", "GFSI compliance", "FSSC 22000 certified facility"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["FSSC 22000 certified since June 2013", "HACCP, GMP, and GFSI compliant food safety systems", "Authentic Southern family recipes dating to 1970", "Highest quality ingredients, made from scratch"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1970 by Bob Hagy -> /about", "Purchased by John Bryan in 2004 -> /about", "John Bryan''s family founded Bryan Foods, Inc. early 1900s -> /about", "Catfish Hotel Restaurant still in business -> /about", "Processing facility built to produce family recipes -> /about", "FSSC 22000 certification since June 2013 -> /about", "HACCP, GMP, GFSI compliance -> /about", "Products: Original, Jalape\u00f1o, Sweet Corn hushpuppies and side dishes -> /", "Located in Savannah, Tennessee -> /", "Authentic Southern recipes -> /", "Highest quality ingredients -> /", "Store locator indicates retail distribution -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Savannah Food Company has been in the food processing business since 1970 when Bob Hagy started making hushpuppies after decades in the restaurant business.", "founded_year": "1970", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='savannah-food-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Saw Logs to Lumber operates from a shop in St. Charles, Missouri, along Highway 94 in the area known as Boschertown. The business was founded in 1994 by Wayne, a Vietnam War veteran who had previously worked as a technical representative at Boeing.

The company runs two sawmills on site, offering custom sawmilling services for both its own inventory and customer-supplied logs. It maintains a stock of over 50,000 board feet of live-edge slabs and more than 800 logs, all sourced from Missouri-native species such as walnut, cherry, oak, and sassafras. In addition to milling, the shop produces custom woodworking items including tables, benches, cutting boards, bartops, paddles, mantel pieces, and swinging benches, and sells hardwood lumber to contractors, builders, and DIY enthusiasts.

Customers range from professional contractors and builders seeking sustainable Missouri hardwood for construction and renovation projects to individual woodworkers and hobbyists looking for unique slabs or custom fabrication. The shop also collaborates with clients who bring their own logs for milling, turning personal timber into finished pieces.

Wayne describes himself as a "Tree Whisperer," emphasizing a philosophy of letting the wood''s natural character guide each cut. The venture began with handmade boats and canoes, expanded into paddle making after a local canoe race, and grew into a full-time operation built on highlighting the art inherent in each log.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom sawmilling", "Live edge slab production", "Custom woodworking", "Milling services for customer-supplied logs", "Hardwood lumber sales", "Custom furniture fabrication (tables, benches, bartops, mantel pieces)", "Paddle making", "Cutting board fabrication", "Swinging bench fabrication", "Cookie slab cutting"], "industries": ["Construction", "Renovation", "Woodworking", "Custom furniture", "DIY enthusiasts"], "materials": ["Missouri-native hardwoods", "Walnut", "Cherry", "Oak", "Sassafras"], "equipment": ["Two sawmills (unspecified models)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1994 by Wayne (Vietnam veteran) -> /about-us", "Location St. Charles, Missouri (Boschertown) -> /about-us, /", "Two sawmills on site -> /", "Over 50,000 board feet of live-edge slabs and 800+ logs inventory -> /", "Missouri-native wood species: walnut, cherry, oak, sassafras -> /, /about-us", "Custom woodworking products: tables, benches, cutting boards, bartops, paddles, mantel pieces, swinging benches -> /", "Lumber sales to contractors, builders, DIY enthusiasts -> /", "Accepts customer-supplied logs for milling -> /", "Veteran-owned -> /about-us", "Company type: manufacturer of wood products -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "At Saw Logs to Lumber, we specialize in custom woodworking and sawmilling.", "founded_year": "1994", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Veteran-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='saw-logs-to-lumber' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Schaumburg Specialties is based in Schaumburg, Illinois. The company does not publicly state its founding year, ownership type, or founder names.

The company manufactures three primary product lines: SHOPCraft for bakery and food production (oven racks, bakery carts, processing tables, dough troughs), KWIKCraft for high-volume food processing (all-welded speed racks for meat, seafood, prepared meals, pet food), and AGRICraft for agriculture and indoor farming (germination racks and custom solutions). It offers custom metal fabrication, welded construction, design collaboration, and bulk product development. The firm also provides maintenance and equipment servicing. Materials include 18-gauge aluminum and stainless steel, with some products featuring anodized coatings. NSF-certified donut basket racks are available.

Customers span industrial bakeries, donut production lines, airline catering commissaries, prepared meal facilities, meat and seafood processors, pet food manufacturers, and indoor farming operations. Named references include David''s Burgers, Bimbo, Illinois State University, Carolina CPL Co-Op, Udi''s (Pinnacle Foods), and operations in Appleton, WI; Elk Grove, IL; and Chapel Hill, NC.

